    {
      "date": "2026-07-19",
      "description": "Widespread Facebook & Instagram Outage",
      "details": "A major outage affected Facebook and Instagram on July 19, 2026, lasting approximately 3.7 hours. Users reported being locked out of accounts, unable to access features, and experiencing ad delivery disruptions. This widespread technical issue would have severely limited ad visibility and user engagement on the platform, leading to poor ad performance. For a brand reliant on Meta ads, this directly translates to lost impressions and conversions, resulting in lower ROAS and higher CPA.",
      "intensity": 3,
      "category": "platform",
      "icon": "🔴",
      "mood_impact": "neutral",
      "feed_dominance": "high",
      "source": "IsDown"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-23",
      "description": "Gas Prices Jump to $4.09/gallon Amid Volatility",
      "details": "The national average for a gallon of regular gasoline surged by 15 cents from the prior week to $4.09 on July 23, 2026. This increase was attributed to rising crude oil prices and volatility along the Strait of Hormuz. Sustained high gas prices erode consumer purchasing power, making discretionary items like specialty food gifts less appealing. This continued financial pressure would likely contribute to suppressed spending, leading to lower ROAS and elevated CPA for a DTC brand.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "medium",
      "source": "AAA Newsroom"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-27",
      "description": "Meta Launches 2026 Holiday Insights Center",
      "details": "Meta introduced its 2026 Holiday Insights Center on July 27, a resource for advertisers to prepare for the upcoming holiday season. While a helpful tool, this launch signals the unofficial start of the competitive holiday ad season. Brands begin planning and increasing budgets, leading to higher CPMs and increased competition in the ad auction. For a gifting-heavy brand, this early ramp-up in competition can prematurely drive down ROAS and increase CPA as ad costs rise.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "seasonal",
      "icon": "🗓️",
      "mood_impact": "neutral",
      "feed_dominance": "low",
      "source": "Meta Business Blog"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-28",
      "description": "Consumer Confidence Declines in July",
      "details": "The Conference Board Consumer Confidence Index decreased by 1.4 points to 90.8 in July, down from 92.2 in June, with the Present Situation Index falling for the third consecutive month. The Expectations Index remained below the recessionary 80.0 threshold, indicating persistent consumer pessimism. This decline in confidence suggests consumers are feeling less secure about the economy and their financial future, leading to reduced discretionary spending. For a premium food gifting brand, this translates to lower conversion intent, negatively impacting ROAS and increasing CPA.",
      "intensity": 3,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "medium",
      "source": "The Conference Board"
    },
    {
